From 5c8bc4d0997fd8bb3c6bbbe014826ad98ec95c41 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mark Shine <72512363+CodeStaple@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 00:11:14 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat(scaleway): bring the CLI to UpCloud parity (#185)

Scaleway had 5 client methods and only stop/start, no credentials command,
and no arm in the shared provider dispatch switches - so node groups, SSH
keys, scaling and upgrades all refused Scaleway clusters even though the
cluster-api mounts those routes for Scaleway in the same loop as UpCloud
(providerapi/clusters.go, lifecycle.go).

internal/client:
- scaleway_credentials.go: list/create API credentials and SSH key
  credentials. The secret key never reaches the command line.
- scaleway_clusters.go: create, preflight, deprovision, worker count,
  scale-workers, k8s version + upgrade, the full node-group surface
  (list/add/scale/instance-type/labels/taints/delete/autoscaling),
  control plane, SSH keys, and the catalog reads
  (locations/instance-types/gateway-types/networks). Written against the
  existing generic provider helpers rather than copying UpCloud's
  per-provider HTTP boilerplate.

cmd:
- scaleway_credentials.go mirroring the Proxmox VE command.
- scaleway_cluster.go gains create, preflight, deprovision, workers,
  k8s-version, the four catalog readers, and control-plane. create and
  preflight share one flag set so they cannot drift; flags left unset are
  omitted from the body so the server's documented defaults apply, and
  --worker-count is tri-state because 0 is legitimate for a
  node-group-only cluster.
- a scaleway arm in the node-group, ssh-keys, scale, upgrade and delete
  dispatch switches, and Scaleway added to the user-facing provider lists
  in those commands' help and refusal text.

Preflight is Scaleway-only: no other provider exposes it as a route. Its
help repeats the documented caveat that it proves availability, not
project hard quota.

Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
